ncluding  normal  trump critic brian class this is a  reference to an anti-semitic  trope when it comes to israel it's all  about  jewish money from the s in defense of  israel  but that same logic isn't applied to  other countries and people of other  national origins when american muslims  are questioned  about whether their loyalty is to the us  or to their  country of family origin for example  whether it's pakistan or saudi arabia or  whatever  we say that's islamophobic rightly so  but when the same is said about the  influence of american jewish money on  politics it's israel and we're supposed  to pretend  like these aren't just two sides of the  same coin now i'll get to  kevin mccarthy in this in a second but  let's uh look at the second tweet  from elon amar first in her second tweet  she quotes someone named bhatia angar  i don't know who that is who said would  love to know  who ilanomar thinks is paying american  politicians to be pro-israel  though i think i can guess bad form  congresswoman  that's the second anti-semitic trope  you've tweeted  and ilana mar quoted that tweet and said  apac the problem here for people who  don't get it  is the implication that americans  support  israel because of money period as  opposed to a host of other cons  considerations  which we can debate whether they're  worthy or not  the conspiracy that all of this refers  to  is the idea of jewish money as a tool  for global domination including the  control of american elected officials  like kevin mccarthy but here's the most  important thing  and this seems to be missing from most  of the arguments i'm seeing about this  on the internet  even if you disagree that the tweets um  are are furthering anti-semitic tropes  that's fine the argument is not valid  because this  all started as a criticism of kevin  mccarthy  who received zero dollars from apac  associates in 2018 so it's just  literally  factually wrong mccarthy was among the  republicans  who were spreading anti-semitic  conspiracy theories  about george soros paying for the  migrant caravan which of course wasn't  true  so i'm not defending mccarthy here he's  horrible  i've been criticizing the guy for years  what i'm pointing out  is that at a logistical level at a  factual level the criticism of mccarthy  as a sort of tool of the israeli lobby  in the united states  is not backed by evidence he received no  donations from  pro-israel pacs in 2018  and this just invalidates even the idea  of the tweet  now is ilanomar personally anti-semitic  i have no idea  i don't think this by itself is evidence  of that  but it's still destructive not only  because anti-semitism  is bad and playing up these stereotypes  is not a good thing  but it forces other democrats to have to  denounce her comments  which just gets in the way of democrats  getting things accomplished  uh whether or not ilana mar is  anti-semitic  nancy pelosi puts out a statement saying  this is bad  she needs to apologize chuck schumer  tweets  that this is uh irresponsible and  offensive  and anti-semitic and then the lana mar  ends up apologizing and more political  capital is spent on this nonsense so  what really needs to be understood here  are a couple different things number one  uh aipac is a more right-wing group and  jews in the u.s  are very very liberal so yeah there are  jews who support  aipac who vote in the united states but  look at evangelical christian support  of aipac and of israel that doesn't even  seem to be mentioned here  it's an important factor but then we get  to the bigger picture  you can recognize that this is playing  on long-time anti-semitic tropes and  still support boycotting israel  for example and the reflexive reaction i  saw for many on the left  to say this can't be anti-semitic  because they felt as though it would in  some way invalidate their support of  boycotting israel  or their opposition to benjamin  netanyahu separate the two things  you can be an opponent 